+/* ---- depth read as colour ---------------------------------------------------
+ * rsx_draw_backend.depth_as_color for a Z24S8 zeta read as A8R8G8B8 (a
+ * renderer rebuilding depth from the bytes; SEGA Rally reads its 2560x1440
+ * scene depth that way every frame). Without it the engine stores the depth
+ * into guest memory: a wait for the GPU, a conversion on the CPU and a decode
+ * and upload of the texture, ~15 MB a frame there. Here the depth is copied
+ * into a buffer, a compute pass makes the bytes eng_zdepth_to_guest would
+ * store (rsx_vk_depth_argb.comp), and they are copied into one RGBA8 image per
+ * depth target, all in command order like the depth snapshot. The engine
+ * samples a crossbar view of that image (vk_eng_surface_view). */
